---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party scientific data, imagery and models (NOT relicensed by SELENORA)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following materials remain under their original NASA / institutional terms
of use and are not redistributed as Apache-2.0 works by this project. SELENORA
code may download, reference or display them at runtime; large binaries and
rasters are generally gitignored and obtained by the user from official sources.

1. NASA / JPL Horizons
   - Solar System Dynamics ephemerides and observer tables
   - https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/
   - https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/horizons.html

2. NASA LOLA / LRO topography (PGDA)
   - Product 78 — High-Resolution LOLA Topography for Lunar South Pole Sites
     https://pgda.gsfc.nasa.gov/products/78
   - Product 90 — A New View of the Lunar South Pole from LOLA
     https://pgda.gsfc.nasa.gov/products/90
   - Barker et al., 2021, Planetary and Space Science 203, 105119
     https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pss.2020.105119

3. NASA / GSFC / Arizona State University — LROC WAC
   - South Pole Summer Mosaic (WAC_ROI_SOUTH_SUMMER) and related LROC products
   - https://data.lroc.im-ldi.com/lroc/view_rdr/WAC_ROI_SOUTH_SUMMER

4. NASA GSFC Scientific Visualization Studio
   - SVS 14959 Moon GLB models (LRO-based)
   - https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14959/

5. Lunar mission coordinate references used in the optional history catalog
   - NASA NSSDC lunar landing sites
     https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/lunar/lunar_sites.html
   - LROC mission site imagery / Wagner et al. 2016 references cited in-catalog
   - NASA CLPS delivery pages and IAU Gazetteer feature centroids for
     planned/failed target regions (not exact unpublished landing ellipses)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open-source dependencies
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SELENORA also depends on third-party open-source libraries (for example FastAPI,
React, Three.js / React Three Fiber, OpenLayers, NumPy, SQLAlchemy, rasterio).
Those packages remain under their own licenses as published by their authors.
See backend/pyproject.toml and frontend/package.json / package-lock.json.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI services
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Optional user-facing explanations may call the DeepSeek API when an operator
supplies a local API key. DeepSeek terms and the key itself are outside this
repository; keys must never be committed.
